{
  "id": "duplicate-kanji-deck-item-confusable",
  "title": "A merged note referenced by a deck item and a confusable pair",
  "covers": [
    "ticket follow-up 5: deck_item n:<loser id> resolves through merged_into_id",
    "confusable: readers resolve merged notes",
    "merge: collision on kanji_literal"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "A has kanji note W for 待 (keyword 'wait') in deck D. B, offline, creates its own note L for 待 (keyword 'await', T+10), adds L to D and confirms L / 持 as look-alikes.",
    "The server merges L into W. L's keyword has a clock (T+10) newer than W's creation value (T+1), so W's keyword becomes 'await': a duplicate's filled-in fields compete by clock like any other write.",
    "B's deck item n:<L> and confusable row keep L's id forever; rows are never rewritten. READERS resolve them through merged_into_id.",
    "So deck D holds two live rows that both mean W. Readers treat them as one item with the smallest (position, item_key): position 512.",
    "The confusable pair reads as (W, 持)."
  ],
